        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): catch unhandled rejections in webhook and ingress worker shutdown",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes Telegram channel shutdown paths that could leave unhandled promise rejections or skip owned cleanup:\n\n1. **Webhook shutdown**: when `bot.stop()` rejected, owned cleanup (transport close, webhook status note, diagnostic heartbeat stop) was skipped.\n2. **Ingress worker shutdown**: repeated `stop()` calls could race teardown, and forced `worker.terminate()` rejections were not observed on the timeout fallback path.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- **Webhook** (`extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts`): wrap `bot.stop()` in `try/catch/finally` so cleanup always runs; route stop failures to `runtime.error`.\n- **Ingress worker** (`extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.ts`): share one in-flight `stopPromise` for idempotent shutdown, catch `postMessage` errors for already-terminated workers, and route forced `worker.terminate()` rejections with `.catch(() => undefined)` on the 15s timeout fallback.\n\nDeliberate non-goals: no transport/streaming/auth behavior changes; no new config surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTelegram webhook abort and ingress-worker shutdown no longer leak unhandled rejections on the covered failure paths, and webhook-owned transport/status/diagnostics cleanup completes even when `bot.stop()` fails.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRebased on current `origin/main` (`471f60bc8481`). Head: `899a1c3af4c6`.\n\n### Forward proof (after fix)\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts -- --run\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts -- --run -t \"does not leak unhandled rejections when shutdown throws\"\n```\n\n```text\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  3 passed (3)\n\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  1 passed | 35 skipped (36)\n```\n\nRegression coverage includes:\n- shared `stopPromise` idempotency\n- forced timeout `terminate()` rejection routed (no `unhandledRejection`)\n- webhook shutdown `finally` cleanup when `bot.stop()` rejects\n\n### Negative control (origin/main prod code + branch tests)\n\nSwap prod files to `origin/main`, run the focused shutdown tests, restore branch prod files:\n\n```bash\ngit show origin/main:extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.ts > /tmp/ingress-main.ts\ngit show origin/main:extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts > /tmp/webhook-main.ts\ncp /tmp/ingress-main.ts extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.ts\ncp /tmp/webhook-main.ts extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts -- --run -t \"idempotent|shutdown throws|terminate rejections|unhandled\"\n```\n\n```text\nTest Files  2 failed (2)\n     Tests  2 failed | 2 passed | 35 skipped (39)\n     Errors  1 error\n```\n\nRestore branch prod files → forward proof passes again.\n\n### What was NOT tested\n\nDid not run a configured live Telegram gateway shutdown with real bot credentials on this machine. Proof is focused mocked lifecycle tests plus negative control on current `origin/main` prod code.\n\nAI-assisted: implementation, tests, and proof were drafted with Cursor agent assistance; validation was run locally with the commands above.",
